{"id":"01a0f17e-8517-7813-ae35-5ac722b60204","slug":"harvard-undergraduate-law-review","name":"Harvard Undergraduate Law Review","acronym":null,"shortDescription":null,"orgType":null,"recognitionStatus":"recognized","activityStatus":"likely_active","joinModes":["application"],"freshmenEligible":true,"joining":{"comp":null,"dues":false,"roles":[],"access":"process","noCuts":false,"general":["application"],"conflicts":[],"firstYears":true,"noExperience":null},"categories":[{"slug":"publications-media","name":"Publications & Media"},{"slug":"law","name":"Law"}],"memberCount":null,"instagramFollowers":1007,"hoursPerWeek":null,"currentCycle":null,"isFixture":false,"completeness":0.5,"sourceCount":14,"lastObservedAt":"2026-10-04T02:39:09.791Z","lastVerifiedAt":"2026-10-01T05:23:03.706Z","eligibleClasses":["first_year","sophomore","junior","senior"],"affiliationScope":"harvard_college","activityConfidence":0.55,"activityReasons":["listed on a current official directory"],"quickLinks":{"website":"https://hulr.org/","instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/harvardundergradlawreview"},"logo":"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/5e17a7262e790958ffa50508/0e2d667a-b11c-4690-88a5-09eee81e1324/favicon.ico?format=100w","pressCount":2,"longDescription":"Such “surrendering” of sovereignty was rooted in the concepts of preemption that long preceded the Cherokee vs Georgia and Worcester vs Georgia cases. “Preemption gave the ‘discovering’ (or, in the US case, its successors) power a monopoly over land transactions with the natives, who were prevented from disposing of their land to any other European power” (p. 391). However, as Wolfe adds, “This semblance of native voluntarism has provided scope for some limited judicial magnanimity in regard to Indian sovereignty. In practice, however, the corollary did not apply. Preemption sanctioned European priority but not Indigenous freedom of choice…The American right to buy always superseded the Indian right not to sell.” Essentially, a power imbalance was conceived and later judicially upheld.","joiningBasis":{"dues":{"rule":"stated_dues","claimIds":["01a0f490-2d91-7f13-b6ed-91608be2d4a1"],"sources":[{"url":"https://soco.college.harvard.edu/club_signup","title":"Student organization directory","sourceType":"harvard_official","observedAt":"2026-09-30T23:04:40.834Z","isFixture":false}]},"access":{"rule":"stated_process","claimIds":["01a0f8da-6ab1-79fd-9979-e75f3d91af96"],"sources":[{"url":"https://hulr.org/join","title":"Join – Harvard Undergraduate Law Review","sourceType":"public_web","observedAt":"2026-10-02T20:49:02.097Z","isFixture":false},{"url":"https://hulr.org/get-involved","title":"Join – Harvard Undergraduate Law Review","sourceType":"public_web","observedAt":"2026-10-02T20:48:59.903Z","isFixture":false}]},"firstYears":{"rule":"open_population","claimIds":["01a0fb48-b50f-7d79-b0be-4150645b1b61"],"sources":[{"url":"https://hulr.org/join","title":"Join – Harvard Undergraduate Law Review","sourceType":"public_web","observedAt":"2026-10-02T20:49:02.097Z","isFixture":false},{"url":"https://hulr.org/get-involved","title":"Join – Harvard Undergraduate Law Review","sourceType":"public_web","observedAt":"2026-10-02T20:48:59.903Z","isFixture":false}]}},"aliases":[{"alias":"Harvard College Law Review","kind":"former"}],"links":[{"kind":"harvard_directory","url":"https://careerservices.fas.harvard.edu/organizations/harvard-undergraduate-law-review","handle":null,"label":"Career center listing","status":"verified","confidence":0,"signals":["listed by an official Harvard source"],"discoveredVia":["harvard_official"],"lastObservedAt":"2026-09-30T08:46:35.646Z"},{"kind":"website","url":"https://hulr.org/","handle":null,"label":null,"status":"probable","confidence":0,"signals":["page title matches the club name"],"discoveredVia":["public_web"],"lastObservedAt":"2026-09-30T12:48:40.544Z"},{"kind":"application_form","url":"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdsonIVL0O76MW61ZOl9H6uFt_uArELCjgu2N3U64